Z||000014||rockcrawl||10-31-2001||07:28 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>....bright beams of light emitting from the box....<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Well if you leave the lid open on the eraser you will see bright light  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> The programmer I use can be seen here <A HREF="http://www.needhams.com/e10.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.needhams.com/e10.html</A>  one of their authorized retailers was selling them on ebay for $175. The eraser cost like $30, I use the same one cooter has. There are a few editing programs like Tunercat, Winbin, Promedit, GME, etc that vary from free to ~$80. The chips can be bought for a few bucks a pop, or you can pull them out of old ECMs or other equipment, they are erasable/reuseable.<P>I just got started in all this within the last year. I'm really glad I did. If you're working with a stock engine, I don't think you'll get much out of it, but it's almost a necessity for doing engine swaps. I got an old pentium 1 or 486 computer (don't remember, it was free) and set it up in my garage just for burning chips. That way I don't need to run into the house to make changes after every test-run and get my good keyboard all greasy.||||reg||1
Z||000015||DRH||10-31-2001||03:02 PM||||OK, this is starting to get my attention. I did a little research and this looks like a great way to support an engine swap.<P>Has anybody done anything with an EPROM emulator? Seems this would make the whole process a lot easier. There's one listed for 89.95 as an accessory to the programmer Cooter is using.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.xtronics.com/memory/EPROM.htm#Emulator" TARGET=_blank>http://www.xtronics.com/memory/EPROM.htm#Emulator</A> <P>Has anyone heard how well it (or another one) works?<P>||||reg||5
Z||000016||terryk||10-31-2001||04:01 PM||||Keep in mind that while emulators are a good way to go, many don't allow on the fly changes. I use the LDTI and it works, but it can't get in and out between memory cycles so the engine will sometimes die and have to be restarted. Sometimes I luck out and the engine just misses for a split second and recovers.<P>Still, if you can live with restarting the engine each time, you can make the changes, save the file and then burn it to an eprom.||||reg||1
Z||000017||tomcat06085||10-31-2001||05:48 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fastback87:<BR><B>Does anyone have any idea how to build an eeprom programmer to program the chip in a fiero or a blank one to put in place of the one in a fiero?  Or does anyone have a way of hooking up the ECM to a laptop to monitor performance??  Just wondering I am pretty handy with a soldering gun and with computers.<P>LMK<P>James</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>I would imagine with flash memory, there should be some easy ways to tweak the code rather than erase it. I've never worked with any flash memory chips, but someone on this board must have. Maybe we could get a programmer from one of the OEM EPROM outfits to give us some tips. It would be neat to soup up a Fiero with a laptop...there's a lot of guys doing it, but they're experts.<BR><P>------------------<BR><BR> <IMG SRC="http://jrreeves.com/images/blckfire.jpg"> <BR>tomcat...Thanks for the help!||||reg||3
Z||000018||terryk||10-31-2001||06:13 PM||||There is a device called a HUD (not the HUD in GTP's) that allows spark and fueling to be changed in real-time. It's a HUGE box that sits on the floor of the passenger side with a display and control box on the dash. <P>It would be nice to duplicate this but it's not practical.<P>All you need is an EPROM programmer (any one that supports the 2732/27C32 (84/86L4 and 85-88 V6) or 27256/27256 (87/88 L4), a handful of EPROMs of the right size and an editor that works with the car of interest. There is only on I know of right now and that's mine but it's only for the V6's. I haven't completed the L4's (sorry Ogre).<P>You read your stock chip into a file using the programmer, load this file into the editor, make the changes, save it to a new file, load that file into the programmer, burn a chip and install it in the car and go check it with a scanner. Repeat until done.<P>That's how it works.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000019||Mark||10-31-2001||06:22 PM||||Terry,<P>What are the "tunable" parameters?  I'm guessing this isn't common knowledge, but surely someone knows the memoy map.  I've just not seen anything myself.||||reg||1
Z||000020||terryk||10-31-2001||09:14 PM||||Much of the important stuff.<P> <p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 11-01-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000021||terryk||11-02-2001||01:55 PM||||*** OPTION FLAGS ***<BR>MANUAL/AUTOMATIC TRANSMISSION<BR>2 BAR/ATM MAP OPTION (BOOST)<P>*** SPARK PARAMETERS ***<BR>SPARK ADVANCE REFERENCE ANGLE<BR>MAIN SPARK ADVANCE TABLE 1 BAR<BR>MAIN SPARK ADVANCE TABLE 2 BAR (BOOST)<BR>SPARK ADVANCE ADDER AT WIDE OPEN THROTTLE (BOOST)<BR>SPARK ADVANCE BASE COOLANT CORRECTION - MAP VS TEMPERATURE<BR>EGR SPARK ADVANCE<P>*** IDLE PARAMETERS ***<BR>PARK/NEUTRAL IDLE RPM<BR>IDLE RPM VS BATTERY VOLTAGE<P>*** FUEL PARAMETERS ***<BR>BASE PULSE VE - RPM VS MAP<BR>BASE PULSE VE - RPM VS MAP - CLOSED THROTTLE (IDLE)<BR>BASE PULSE VE VS RPM (BOOST)<BR>INJECTOR OFFSET VS BASE PULSE WIDTH<BR>POWER ENRICHMENT RPM THRESHOLD (BOOST)<BR>TPS% THROTTLE ANGLE CHANGE FOR POWER ENRICHMENT<BR>THROTTLE HYSTERESIS FOR POWER ENRICHMENT<BR>POWER ENRICHMENT AIR/FUEL RATIO<BR>DECEL FUEL CUTOFF MPH<BR>DECEL FUEL CUTOFF RPM<BR>DECEL ENLEANMENT TPS% THROTTLE ANGLE<BR>COLD ENGINE AFR VS COOLANT AND MAP<P>*** 2 BAR/TURBO ADJUSTABLE PARAMETERS ***<BR>POWER ENRICHMENT RPM THRESHOLD (BOOST)<BR>DELTA MAP THRESHOLD TO ENABLE ACCELERATION ENRICHMENT (BOOST)<BR>DELTA TPS THRESHOLD TO DOUBLE THE DELTA MAP THRESHOLD ((BOOST)<BR>TPS THRESHOLD FOR MAP CONTRIBUTION (BOOST)<BR>DELTA TPS THRESHOLD FOR ACCELERATION ENRICHMENT (BOOST)<BR>DECEL ENLEANMENT DELTA MANIFOLD PRESSURE THRESHOLD (BOOST)<BR>DECEL ENLEANMENT DELTA MANIFOLD PRESSURE THRESHOLD (BOOST)<BR>MANIFOLD PRESSURE TO ENABLE DECEL FUEL CUTOFF (BOOST)<BR>DECEL FUEL CUTOFF MULTIPLIER STEP VALUE (BOOST)<BR>MANIFOLD PRESSURE TO ENABLE BOOST MODE (BOOST)<BR>MANIFOLD PRESSURE TO ENABLE FUEL SHUTOFF (BOOST)<BR>PRIMARY POWER ENRICHMENT THRESHOLD (BOOST)<BR>SECONDARY POWER ENRICHMENT THRESHOLD (BOOST)<BR>SECONDARY POWER ENRICHMENT TPS LOAD THRESHOLD (BOOST)<BR>ACCELERATION ENRICHMENT DELTA CONTRIBUTION VS DELTA MAP (BOOST)<BR>ACCELERATION DELTA THROTTLE CONTRIBUTION VS 8*DETLA THROTTLE (BOOST)<BR>BASE PULSE MULITPLIER VS BOOST (BOOST)<P>*** FUEL SHUTOFF PARAMETERS ***<BR>HIGH RPM FUEL RESTORE<BR>HIGH MPH FUEL SHUTOFF<P>*** INJECTOR PARAMETERS ***<BR>BASE PULSE INJECTOR CONSTANT FOR EGR AT 0% FLOW (KNEGRCST)<P>*** TORQUE CONVERTER PARAMETERS ***<BR>TCC LOWER LOCK TEMPERATURE<BR>TCC HYSTERISIS FOR 1/2 COAST<BR>TCC ROAD COAST SPEED<BR>TCC LOW-MPH COAST LOAD LIMIT<BR>TCC HIGH-MPH COAST LOAD LIMIT<BR>DELAY TCC LOCKUP TIME AFTER TCC IS ENABLED<BR>TCC ROAD SPEED UPPER LIMIT FOR LOCK<BR>TCC UPPER/LOWER LOAD LIMIT<P>*** SHIFT LIGHT PARAMETERS ***<BR>N/V RATIO FOR HIGH GEAR TO BE UPSHIFTED<BR>ENGINE SPEED TOLERANCE FOR HIGHEST GEAR<BR>IN-GEAR DELAY TIME FOR FIRST GEAR<BR>IN-GEAR DELAY TIME FOR 2ND, 3RD, 4TH, AND 5TH GEAR<BR>N/V RATIO FOR 2ND HIGHEST GEAR TO BE UPSHIFTED<BR>ENGINE SPEED TOLERANCE FOR 2ND HIGHEST GEAR<BR>MINIMUM RPM TO ALLOW SHIFT TO NEXT HIGHEST GEAR<BR>MAXIMUM MAP TO ALLOW SHIFT TO NEXT HIGHEST GEAR<BR>N/V RATIO FOR 3RD HIGHEST GEAR TO BE UPSHIFTED<BR>ENGINE SPEED TOLERANCE FOR 3RD HIGHEST GEAR<BR>MINIMUM RPM TO ALLOW SHIFT TO NEXT HIGHEST GEAR (4TH)<BR>MAXIMUM MAP TO ALLOW SHIFT TO NEXT HIGHEST GEAR (4TH)<BR>N/V RATIO FOR 4TH  GEAR<BR>ENGINE SPEED TOLERANCE FOR 4TH HIGHEST GEAR<BR>MINIMUM RPM TO ALLOW SHIFT TO NEXT HIGHEST GEAR (5TH)<BR>MAXIMUM MAP TO ALLOW SHIFT TO NEXT HIGHEST GEAR (5TH)<BR>*** EGR PARAMETERS ***<BR>EGR ENABLE TEMPERATURE<BR>TPS% THROTTLE ANGLE FOR EGR OFF/ON<BR>BASE PULSE FOR EGR FLOW RATE (F28A)<BR>DIAG UPPER LIMIT FOR EGR DUTY CYCLE (BOOST)<P>*** A/C PARAMETERS ***<BR>TPS% TO DISABLE A/C CLUTCH<P>||||reg||1
